# TravelXP Client Environment Variables
VITE_API_URL="http://localhost:5000/api/v1"

# Client-side Google Maps JavaScript API Key (browser-restricted)
# Instructions to configure locally:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create or select a project, then navigate to APIs & Services > Credentials.
# 3. Create an API Key and restrict it to HTTP referrers: http://localhost:5173/* (and your production domain).
# 4. In APIs & Services > Library, enable:
#    - "Maps JavaScript API" (for vector rendering and markers)
#    - "Places API" (for destination search and autocomplete)
# 5. Copy the key and set it in your local client/.env file as:
#    VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY="your-google-maps-api-key-here"
#
# Note: If this variable is left empty, TravelXP automatically falls back gracefully
# to the high-performance Carto Voyager cultural tile layer without breaking or hanging.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=""
